-- title:
--   Regularity at the cusp ∞ of the pole chart over ℤ₍ₚ₎
-- statement:
--   Let $M \ge 1$ be an integer and $p$ a prime, and write $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of the rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. Let $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M` be the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}((\mathfrak q))$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the $\mathfrak q$-expansions of $j(\mathfrak q^d)$ for the nonzero divisors $d \mid M$, and let `chartAlgInf M p` be the subalgebra of $F$ of elements integral over the $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-subalgebra generated by $1/j$, with `jInvChartInf M p` the element $1/j$ of it. Let $\mathfrak m$ be a prime ideal of `chartAlgInf M p` which is assumed to consist exactly of those $b$ whose Laurent expansion has $\mathfrak q^0$-coefficient of the form $p\,c$ with $c \in \mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$. Let $B_{\mathfrak m}$ be any commutative `chartAlgInf M p`-algebra that is a localisation of `chartAlgInf M p` at $\mathfrak m$. Then $B_{\mathfrak m}$ is a regular local ring, its Krull dimension is $2$, and the ideal of $B_{\mathfrak m}$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak m$ is generated by the images of $p$ and of $1/j$.
--
--   This is the assertion that the cusp $\infty$ of $X_0(M)$, described through the pole chart given by the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[1/j]$ in the function field, reduces to a point at which the model is smooth over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ for every $M$ and every prime $p$, including $p \mid M$, with regular parameters $p$ and $1/j$. It is used in the construction of sections through the smooth locus of the Igusa scheme, in [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_mem_and_smooth_of_section_cuspInf_of_asIdeal_ne_bot`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_mem_and_smooth_of_section_cuspInf_of_asIdeal_ne_bot) and [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_smoothLocus_maximal_and_section_mem`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_smoothLocus_maximal_and_section_mem).
